o keep!\n- **Play J1**: Red Dragon \u2014 same logic as J3. No current pung, but dragons are always valuable for scoring.\n\nKey Insight: I already have two melds: [T5,T5,T5] (pung) and [W5,W6,W7] (chow). Remaining goal is to complete two more melds and a pair. Best chance is to aim for:\n- **Dragon Pung** (J1/J3) \u2013 both singletons now.\n- **Wind Pung** \u2013 especially F2 (South), where I already have two copies and only one is unaccounted for. Very promising!\n\nReason: Among all options, **F2** is the most strategic to *keep*, not discard, because:\n- I already have **two F2s**, and only **one F2 remains unshown** \u2192 high chance it's still in the wall or draw pile.\n- Completing a **pung of F2 (South Wind)** would give me **2 points (Prevalent Wind bonus)**.\n- Discarding one of my two F2s now would destroy this opportunity permanently.\n- All other candidates (like J1, J3, F1) are either singleton honors or harder to pair.\n\nTherefore, among the valid actions, **discarding F2 is the worst move** \u2014 but since it's listed as a choice, I must avoid it. Instead, I should eliminate least useful honor.\n\nBetween **J1** and **J3**, both are single dragon tiles. But J2 has 4 copies unshown \u2014 meaning no one has claimed it much \u2014 possibly safe. J3 has only 1 left, and I have one \u2014 so likely rare. J1 has 3 unshown \u2014 more available. So **J1 is safer to discard**.\n\nBut wait \u2014 check history: previous player played J1, next player played J3 \u2014 both dragons are being discarded freely. Likely no one is building them.\n\nStill, **F2 is too valuable to discard** \u2014 keep it for pung.\n\nBest discard: **J3** \u2014 slightly rarer than J1, but both are equally unused. Since J3 appears only once in unshown and I have one, playing it doesn\u2019t hurt much. But actually, **F1** is also weak \u2014 only one copy unshown, and I have one. Seat wind is good, but no sign of collecting F1.\n\nWait \u2014 look at **valid actions**: I can play